{"width":1920,"height":2688,"lines":[{"text":"Apricot Bavarian","bbox":[753,1157,392,48],"confidence":0.993},{"text":"12 cup cold water","bbox":[1014,1217,292,44],"confidence":0.995},{"text":"1 pint milk","bbox":[355,1217,193,46],"confidence":1.0},{"text":"1 cup apricot pulp","bbox":[1011,1258,301,36],"confidence":0.991},{"text":"2 eggs","bbox":[355,1256,114,45],"confidence":0.955},{"text":"1 teaspoon lemon extract","bbox":[1011,1295,408,36],"confidence":1.0},{"text":"1/2 cup sugar","bbox":[359,1293,215,43],"confidence":0.934},{"text":"112 tablespoons granulated gelatine 12 cup cream","bbox":[358,1327,875,48],"confidence":0.974},{"text":"Scald the milk and pour it over the egg yolks which have been","bbox":[292,1372,1351,60],"confidence":0.993},{"text":"beaten with the sugar; return to the saucepan (double boiler) and","bbox":[250,1428,1392,57],"confidence":0.996},{"text":"cook until thickened. Soften the gelatine in the cold water, add this","bbox":[248,1480,1395,57],"confidence":0.985},{"text":"to the custard with the apricot pulp and set aside to cool. Beat in","bbox":[249,1531,1394,61],"confidence":0.999},{"text":"the flavoring, cream whipped until stiff, and stiffly beaten egg whites.","bbox":[250,1586,1390,57],"confidence":0.996},{"text":"Turn into a mold previously dipped into cold water; chill, unmold","bbox":[249,1635,1394,61],"confidence":0.991},{"text":"and serve plain or with additional fruit.","bbox":[248,1688,834,64],"confidence":0.998},{"text":"Apricot Cobbler","bbox":[765,1811,365,52],"confidence":1.0},{"text":"2 eggs","bbox":[1005,1873,114,44],"confidence":0.925},{"text":"1 can apricots or 1 quart stewed,","bbox":[358,1873,538,48],"confidence":1.0},{"text":"11 cups flour","bbox":[1009,1912,234,40],"confidence":0.993},{"text":"sweetened, dried or fresh","bbox":[431,1912,410,45],"confidence":1.0},{"text":"1/3 teaspoon salt","bbox":[1012,1949,264,40],"confidence":0.963},{"text":"apricots","bbox":[431,1953,140,39],"confidence":1.0},{"text":"11/2 teaspoons Rumford Baking","bbox":[1012,1986,511,40],"confidence":0.969},{"text":"3 tablespoons butter","bbox":[359,1986,339,44],"confidence":1.0},{"text":"Powder","bbox":[1080,2021,135,42],"confidence":1.0},{"text":"1/2 cup milk","bbox":[679,2019,200,50],"confidence":0.952},{"text":"1/3 cup sugar","bbox":[362,2028,213,40],"confidence":0.923},{"text":"Place the fruit, which should be quite juicy, in a baking dish.","bbox":[294,2077,1347,61],"confidence":1.0},{"text":"Cream the butter and sugar, add the beaten eggs, then the flour,","bbox":[250,2134,1390,57],"confidence":0.997},{"text":"salt and baking powder sifted together, alternately with the milk.","bbox":[248,2182,1396,65],"confidence":1.0},{"text":"Pour over the fruit and bake thirty to thirty-five minutes in a hot","bbox":[247,2237,1397,61],"confidence":0.999},{"text":"oven—375-400 degrees F. Serve plain or with light cream.","bbox":[245,2288,1230,69],"confidence":0.987},{"text":"9","bbox":[1616,2400,29,40],"confidence":1.0},{"text":"ALL MEASUREMENTS ARE LEVEL","bbox":[588,2395,712,53],"confidence":1.0}]}